@startuml Episode Management Workflow
!theme plain
title SABER Episode Management Workflow

actor Client
participant "AgentUnderTest" as Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "TaskManager" as TM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM
participant "Task" as T
participant "PolicyManager" as PM
participant "MCPServer" as MCP

== Episode Initialization ==

Client -> SM: start_task_episode(session_id, task_id)
SM -> TM: reset(session_id, task_id)
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: None (no active episode)
TM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "reset") [if exists]
TM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
TM -> TM: start_episode(session_id, task_id)
TM -> EM: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
EM -> EM: create Episode object
EM -> EM: store in active_episodes[session_id]
EM --> TM: episode
TM -> T: initialize_episode(episode)
T -> T: set entry subtasks to in_progress
T -> T: set other subtasks to not_visited
TM --> SM: episode

== Task Context & Policy Gathering ==

SM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
TM --> SM: current_task
SM -> PM: get_policy()
PM --> SM: policy_document
SM -> PM: get_guidelines()
PM --> SM: guidelines
SM -> PM: get_hints()
PM --> SM: context_hints

note right of SM
  SessionManager gathers:
  - Current task details
  - Domain policy document
  - Agent guidelines
  - Context hints
end note

SM -> Client: episode_info + task_context + policy + guidelines + hints

== Agent Initialization ==

Client -> Agent: initialize(task_context, policy, guidelines, hints)
Agent -> Agent: analyze task requirements
Agent -> Agent: plan initial approach
Agent --> Client: ready_for_commands

== Command Execution & RL Step ==

Agent -> Agent: analyze current state
Agent -> Agent: generate next command
Agent -> Client: execute_command(command_name, parameters)
Client -> SM: execute_command(session_id, command_name, parameters)
SM -> SM: create Action(command_name, parameters)
SM -> MCP: execute_command(command_name, parameters)
MCP --> SM: CommandResult

note right of SM
  Integration Point:
  Action + CommandResult
end note

SM -> TM: step(session_id, action, command_result)
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: episode
TM -> TM: get_task(episode.task_id)
TM -> EM: step(session_id, action, command_result, current_objective)

== EpisodeManager Step Processing ==

EM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM -> EM: create_step(episode, action, command_result)
EM -> EM: extract command from action
EM -> EM: create Step object
EM -> EM: add step to episode
EM -> EM: update_episode_state(episode, step)
EM --> TM: Step
TM -> T: check_episode_progression(episode, step)

== Task Progression Logic ==

T -> T: check subtask progression
T -> T: update episode subtask states
loop for each in_progress subtask
    T -> T: subtask.check_exit_conditions(episode)
    note right of T
      Checks if required commands
      were executed in episode
    end note
end
loop for each not_visited subtask
    T -> T: subtask.check_entry_conditions(episode)
    note right of T
      Checks if dependencies
      are completed
    end note
end
T -> T: update step subtask states
T -> T: log progression changes

TM -> TM: check if episode is complete
TM -> TM: set step.done = completion_status
TM --> SM: Step
SM -> Client: CommandResult + Step

== Agent Response & Next Command Generation ==

Client -> Agent: command_result + step_info
Agent -> Agent: analyze command results
Agent -> Agent: update internal state
Agent -> Agent: assess task progress

alt if episode not complete
    Agent -> Agent: generate next command
    Agent -> Client: execute_command(next_command, parameters)
    note right of Agent
      Agent continuously processes
      results and generates next
      commands until episode complete
    end note
else episode complete
    Agent -> Agent: finalize task completion
    Agent -> Client: episode_complete_signal
end

== Episode Completion ==

note over SM, EM
  When episode is complete (all subtasks done)
end note

Client -> SM: end_session(session_id)
SM -> TM: end_episode(session_id, "session_ended")
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: episode
TM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "session_ended")
EM -> EM: episode.end_time = now()
EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED/FAILED
EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = reason
EM -> EM: delete from active_episodes
EM --> TM: episode
TM --> SM: episode
SM -> Client: session_ended
Client -> Agent: cleanup()

note over Client, Agent
  Clear interface boundaries:
  - Client handles all server communication
  - AgentUnderTest focuses on task execution
  - Agent receives structured context and generates commands
  - Client manages session lifecycle
end note

@enduml
